  {
   "nid": 1790070935881,
   "field": "Lecture Notes",
   "mode": "append_missing",
   "value": "Ex: <i>laa</i> (no) — laam joins alif from the right — and since it never joins forward, the word simply ends [sound:arabic_khouri_laa.mp3]<br><br><span style='font-size:28px'>‎لا</span><br><br>Dr. Khouri says it: [sound:arabic_khouri_letter_alif.mp3]"
  },
  {
   "nid": 1789129142455,
   "field": "Back Extra",
   "mode": "append_missing",
   "value": "Ex: <i>baab</i> (door) — baa opens the word and reaches forward to join alif [sound:arabic_khouri_baab.mp3]<br><br><span style='font-size:28px'>‎باب</span><br><br>Dr. Khouri says it: [sound:arabic_khouri_letter_baa.mp3]"
  },
  {
   "nid": 1789129142621,
   "field": "Back Extra",
   "mode": "append_missing",
   "value": "Ex: <i>khubz</i> (bread) — khaa joins baa from the right, and baa reaches forward to zaay [sound:arabic_lingco_u4vst_01.mp3]<br><br><span style='font-size:28px'>‎خُبْز</span><br><br>Dr. Khouri says it: [sound:arabic_khouri_letter_baa.mp3]"
  },
  {
   "nid": 1789129142806,
   "field": "Back Extra",
   "mode": "append_missing",
   "value": "Ex: <i>tuHibb</i> (you love / like) — Haa joins baa from the right, and the word ends there [sound:arabic_khouri_0908_tuhibb.mp3]<br><br><span style='font-size:28px'>‎تُحِبّ</span><br><br>Dr. Khouri says it: [sound:arabic_khouri_letter_baa.mp3]"
  },
  {
   "nid": 1789129142971,
   "field": "Back Extra",
   "mode": "append_missing",
   "value": "Ex: <i>tuHibb</i> (you love / like) — taa opens the word and reaches forward to join Haa [sound:arabic_khouri_0908_tuhibb.mp3]<br><br><span style='font-size:28px'>‎تُحِبّ</span>"
  },
  {
   "nid": 1789129143213,
   "field": "Back Extra",
   "mode": "append_missing",
   "value": "Ex: <i>kitaab</i> (book) — kaaf joins taa from the right, and taa reaches forward to alif [sound:arabcram_u03_0038_formal.mp3]<br><br><span style='font-size:28px'>‎كِتاب</span>"
  },
  {
   "nid": 1789129143393,
   "field": "Back Extra",
   "mode": "append_missing",
   "value": "Ex: <i>bayt</i> (house) — yaa joins taa from the right, and the word ends there [sound:arabcram_u03_0034_formal.mp3]<br><br><span style='font-size:28px'>‎بَيْت</span>"
  },
  {
   "nid": 1789129143565,
   "field": "Back Extra",
   "mode": "append_missing",
   "value": "Ex: <i>ithnaan</i> (two) — alif never joins forward, so thaa starts fresh and reaches forward to join nuun [sound:arabic_khouri_0922_ithnaan.mp3]<br><br><span style='font-size:28px'>‎اِثْنان</span>"
  },
  {
   "nid": 1789129143745,
   "field": "Back Extra",
   "mode": "append_missing",
   "value": "Ex: <i>juthath</i> (corpses, dead bodies) — jiim joins thaa from the right, and thaa reaches forward to thaa [sound:arabic_lingco_u3d1_05.mp3]<br><br><span style='font-size:28px'>‎جُثَث</span>"
  },
  {
   "nid": 1789129143931,
   "field": "Back Extra",
   "mode": "append_missing",
   "value": "Ex: <i>Hayth</i> (where (the place where)) — yaa joins thaa from the right, and the word ends there [sound:arabic_khouri_0917_hayth.mp3]<br><br><span style='font-size:28px'>‎حَيْث</span>"
  },
  {
   "nid": 1789129144110,
   "field": "Back Extra",
   "mode": "append_missing",
   "value": "Ex: <i>yaa</i> (O — you are addressing someone directly) — yaa opens the word and reaches forward to join alif [sound:arabcram_u03_0043_formal.mp3]<br><br><span style='font-size:28px'>‎يا</span>"
  },
  {
   "nid": 1789129144281,
   "field": "Back Extra",
   "mode": "append_missing",
   "value": "Ex: <i>bayt</i> (house) — baa joins yaa from the right, and yaa reaches forward to taa [sound:arabcram_u03_0034_formal.mp3]<br><br><span style='font-size:28px'>‎بَيْت</span>"
  },
  {
   "nid": 1789129144455,
   "field": "Back Extra",
   "mode": "append_missing",
   "value": "Ex: <i>fii</i> (in) — faa joins yaa from the right, and the word ends there [sound:arabic_vocab_u1_09_fii_formal.mp3]<br><br><span style='font-size:28px'>‎في</span>"
  },
  {
   "nid": 1789129144676,
   "field": "Back Extra",
   "mode": "append_missing",
   "value": "Ex: <i>huwa</i> (he; it) — haa joins waaw from the right — and since it never joins forward, the word simply ends [sound:arabic_lingco_u4vst_16.mp3]<br><br><span style='font-size:28px'>‎هُوَ</span>"
  },
  {
   "nid": 1790070936003,
   "field": "Lecture Notes",
   "mode": "append_missing",
   "value": "Ex: <i>jaar</i> (neighbor) — jiim opens the word and reaches forward to join alif [sound:arabic_khouri_0929_jaar.mp3]<br><br><span style='font-size:28px'>‎جار</span><br><br>Dr. Khouri says it: [sound:arabic_khouri_letter_jiim.mp3]"
  },
  {
   "nid": 1790070936124,
   "field": "Lecture Notes",
   "mode": "append_missing",
   "value": "Ex: <i>Hijaab</i> (veil, head covering) — Haa joins jiim from the right, and jiim reaches forward to alif [sound:arabcram_u03_0033_formal.mp3]<br><br><span style='font-size:28px'>‎حِجاب</span><br><br>Dr. Khouri says it: [sound:arabic_khouri_letter_jiim.mp3]"
  },
  {
   "nid": 1790070936216,
   "field": "Lecture Notes",
   "mode": "append_missing",
   "value": "Ex: <i>beej</i> (beige) — yaa joins jiim from the right, and the word ends there [sound:arabic_khouri_0908_beej.mp3]<br><br><span style='font-size:28px'>‎بيج</span><br><br>Dr. Khouri says it: [sound:arabic_khouri_letter_jiim.mp3]"
  },
  {
   "nid": 1790070936314,
   "field": "Lecture Notes",
   "mode": "append_missing",
   "value": "Ex: <i>uHibb</i> (I love; I like) — hamza on alif never joins forward, so Haa starts fresh and reaches forward to join baa [sound:arabic_lingco_u4vst_28.mp3]<br><br><span style='font-size:28px'>‎أُحِبّ</span>"
  },
  {
   "nid": 1790070936406,
   "field": "Lecture Notes",
   "mode": "append_missing",
   "value": "Ex: <i>tuHibb</i> (you love / like) — taa joins Haa from the right, and Haa reaches forward to baa [sound:arabic_khouri_0908_tuhibb.mp3]<br><br><span style='font-size:28px'>‎تُحِبّ</span>"
  },
  {
   "nid": 1790070936498,
   "field": "Lecture Notes",
   "mode": "append_missing",
   "value": "Ex: <i>mniiH</i> (good, fine) — yaa joins Haa from the right, and the word ends there [sound:arabic_lingco_u3vs_20.mp3]<br><br><span style='font-size:28px'>‎منيح</span>"
  },
  {
   "nid": 1790070936593,
   "field": "Lecture Notes",
   "mode": "append_missing",
   "value": "Ex: <i>khubz</i> (bread) — khaa opens the word and reaches forward to join baa [sound:arabic_lingco_u4vst_01.mp3]<br><br><span style='font-size:28px'>‎خُبْز</span>"
  },
  {
   "nid": 1790070936687,
   "field": "Lecture Notes",
   "mode": "append_missing",
   "value": "Ex: <i>bi-khayr</i> (good, well) — baa joins khaa from the right, and khaa reaches forward to yaa [sound:arabcram_u03_0051_formal.mp3]<br><br><span style='font-size:28px'>‎بِخَير</span>"
  },
  {
   "nid": 1790070936781,
   "field": "Lecture Notes",
   "mode": "append_missing",
   "value": "Ex: <i>baTTiikh</i> (watermelon) — yaa joins khaa from the right, and the word ends there [sound:arabic_khouri_0910_battiikh.mp3]<br><br><span style='font-size:28px'>‎بِطّيخ</span>"
  },
